{"name":"Fabric of Love","hex":"#aa1177","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fabric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edifice or building.","The act of constructing, construction, fabrication."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabric"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Textile","blocks":[{"text":"A textile is any of various fibre-based materials, including fibres, yarns, filaments, threads, and different types of fabric. Originally, textiles were woven; however, weaving is not the only manufacturing method, and many other methods were later developed to form textile structures based on their intended use. Knitting and non-woven are other popular types of fabric manufacturing. In the contemporary world, textiles satisfy the material needs for versatile applications, from simple daily clothing to bulletproof jackets, spacesuits, doctor's gowns and technical applications like geotextiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Warp_in_Progress.jpg/330px-Warp_in_Progress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textile"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/1280px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg/500px-Flores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Handmade floral patterns on textiles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlores_y_colores_hechos_a_mano.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/1280px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant%27s_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrooklyn_Museum_-_Cloth_Merchant's_Shop_-_Basarat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Museum_of_Lincolnshire_Life%2C_Lincoln%2C_England_-_DSCF1759.JPG/500px-Museum_of_Lincolnshire_Life%2C_Lincoln%2C_England_-_DSCF1759.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/